{"availability":"available","full":"marcominerva/AgentPlayground","name":"AgentPlayground","description":"A Blazor Web App playground for quickly testing agents built with Microsoft Agent Framework","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":21,"forks":3,"created":"2023-06-20T15:10:59Z","updated":"2026-10-02T14:21:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["agent-framework","aspnetcore","azure-openai","blazor","blazor-application","c-sharp","hacktoberfest","openai","visual-studio"],"demo":"https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet/10.0","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:13.598Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:13.598Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:13.598Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:36:13.598Z","stars":21,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Blazor Web App playground for quickly testing agents built with Microsoft Agent Framework. The project provides a ready-to-use chat UI, session handling, streaming responses, reasoning display, function-call visibility, and token-usage details, so you can focus on defining and experimenting with your agent.","The goal is to provide a lightweight playground for local agent experiments. Instead of rebuilding a chat UI and streaming pipeline for every test, you can configure the PlaygroundAgent and start interacting with it from the browser.","The default agent is registered in Program.cs with the name PlaygroundAgent. The AgentService is already wired to that agent and its session store, and exposes a streaming method that the Blazor UI consumes."],"features":["Define a Microsoft Agent Framework agent in one place: Program.cs","Test the agent immediately through a Blazor chat interface","Stream answers as they are generated","Show reasoning output when the model provides it","Show function/tool calls made by the agent"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marcominerva/AgentPlayground/blob/master/RE